  "generalProof": "If d=l-1 is even, d|2e but d does not divide e forces e=(2k+1)d/2. If e is even, d/2 must be even, so d is divisible by 4 and l=1 mod4. The quadratic subfield is Q(sqrt(l)); for l=3 mod4 the exceptional even-e case does not occur.",
